我非常喜欢这个节目。

00:52:01.815 --> 00:52:02.580
Here we go.
开始了。

00:52:02.580 --> 00:52:04.177
This one's from Daniel.
这是丹尼尔发来的。

00:52:04.177 --> 00:52:05.219
He's from Peru.
他来自秘鲁。

00:52:05.219 --> 00:52:07.789
He says, him, he's my comfort series.
他说，他，他是我的安慰系列。

00:52:07.789 --> 00:52:11.610
I watch it when I'm happy, when I am sad, when I'm mad.
我开心的时候看，悲伤的时候看，生气的时候看。

00:52:11.610 --> 00:52:13.858
I want to thank you Craig and Carter.
我要感谢克雷格和卡特。

00:52:13.858 --> 00:52:20.483
I'm adding that for creating this piece of art and you, Josh, for giving your heart and soul to this project.
我添加这一点是为了创造这件艺术品，而你，乔什，为这个项目付出了你的心和灵魂。

00:52:20.483 --> 00:52:24.798
I own a little music box that plays love Vian Rose and own a ducky tie.
我有一个小音乐盒，可以播放维安·罗斯（Vian Rose）的歌曲，还有一条小领带。

00:52:24.798 --> 00:52:26.804
This one's from Julia in Austria.
这是来自奥地利的朱莉娅。

00:52:26.804 --> 00:52:38.959
The show helped me through some of the harder times, especially my quarter-life crisis, when seemingly all of my friends have been in relationships and I was still on my own trying to figure out life.
这个节目帮助我度过了一些困难时期，尤其是我的四分之一人生危机，当时我的所有朋友似乎都已经恋爱了，而我仍然独自试图弄清楚生活。

00:52:38.960 --> 00:52:46.440
From Danella, from Chile, she wrote to us in Spanish, and we got it Google translated, which led to this.
来自智利的达内拉（Danella）用西班牙语给我们写信，我们得到了谷歌翻译，这导致了这一点。

00:52:46.440 --> 00:52:49.159
I started watching this series about two or three years ago.
我大约两三年前开始看这个系列。

00:52:49.159 --> 00:52:58.360
My husband recommended it to me and I became obsessed with each of the episodes, the story, how the stories were woven in time, the flashbacks of the seasons, the pineapple, the pumpkin, et cetera.
我丈夫向我推荐了它，我开始沉迷于每一集、故事、故事如何及时编织、季节的闪回、菠萝、南瓜等等。

00:52:58.360 --> 00:53:03.838
My obsession has been so great that my husband and I agreed that we would only watch it once a year.
我的痴迷是如此之大，以至于我和丈夫同意我们每年只看一次。

00:53:03.838 --> 00:53:06.193
That's better English than I have speaking.
这英语比我说的好。

00:53:06.193 --> 00:53:06.851
So good job.
干得好。

00:53:06.851 --> 00:53:09.370
Everybody watch the entire series once a year.
每个人每年都会观看整个系列一次。

00:53:09.370 --> 00:53:10.137
Is that right?
是这样吗？

00:53:10.137 --> 00:53:10.795
Interesting.
有趣的。

00:53:10.795 --> 00:53:13.370
Well, I wonder how many times she's up to them.
好吧，我想知道她有多少次是这样的。

00:53:13.369 --> 00:53:14.161
What does that equal?
那等于什么？

00:53:14.161 --> 00:53:16.010
And how long it takes to watch the entire series?
看完整个系列需要多长时间？

00:53:16.809 --> 00:53:17.309
Right.
正确的。

00:53:17.309 --> 00:53:20.173
Because if you watched one a day, it would be two thirds of a year.
因为如果每天看一次，就相当于一年的三分之二。

00:53:21.019 --> 00:53:22.619
That's a good point.
这是一个很好的观点。

00:53:22.619 --> 00:53:27.260
So she's not minimizing it that much if she's watching it.
所以如果她在看的话，她不会把它最小化那么多。

00:53:27.260 --> 00:53:28.073
of that right?
对吗？

00:53:28.073 --> 00:53:28.573
Okay.
好的。

00:53:28.573 --> 00:53:29.386
But I love it.
但我喜欢它。

00:53:29.386 --> 00:53:31.768
This one is from Amanda in New York City.
这是来自纽约市的阿曼达。

00:53:31.768 --> 00:53:36.358
There are no words to describe with the show how I met your mother means to me.
无法用言语来形容这部剧对我来说意味着什么。

00:53:36.358 --> 00:53:37.230
But I will try.
但我会尝试。

00:53:37.230 --> 00:53:45.712
I was 19 when I watched the show for the first time, which was only seven months ago, showed to me by my friend Samantha, who claimed I'd love it.
我第一次观看这个节目时才 19 岁，那是在七个月前，我的朋友萨曼莎向我展示了这个节目，她声称我会喜欢它。

00:53:45.712 --> 00:53:51.115
I didn't believe her at first, but that night we watched half of season one and I was hooked.
一开始我并不相信她，但那天晚上我们看了第一季的一半，我就被迷住了。

00:53:51.115 --> 00:53:56.518
I think how I met your mother taught me it was okay to take time to get where you need to be.
我想我与你母亲的相遇告诉我，花时间去到达你需要去的地方是可以的。

00:53:56.518 --> 00:54:03.722
Finding comedy in serious situations, especially the way the show executed it, is a metaphor that I've used in my real life.
在严肃的情况下寻找喜剧，尤其是节目的执行方式，是我在现实生活中使用的一个比喻。

00:54:03.722 --> 00:54:07.731
You need to find the humor, enjoy, and even the most dire situations.
你需要找到幽默、享受，甚至是最可怕的情况。

00:54:07.731 --> 00:54:10.985
That really is the only way you can truly get past them.
这确实是你真正能够克服它们的唯一方法。

00:54:10.985 --> 00:54:18.828
I can say with my full chest that this show saved me from a really hard time in my life and taught me it was okay and to never give up.
我可以满怀信心地说，这部剧把我从人生中最艰难的时刻救了出来，并教会我一切都好，永远不要放弃。

00:54:18.828 --> 00:54:24.754
Because in the end, you'll end up where you need to be, and most importantly, You'll be happy with it.
因为最终，你会到达你需要到达的地方，最重要的是，你会对此感到满意。

00:54:24.754 --> 00:54:27.659
This show is the definition of trust, the process.
这个节目是信任的定义，过程。

00:54:27.449 --> 00:54:28.897
And I adore it very much.
我非常喜欢它。

00:54:28.897 --> 00:54:31.849
Carter and Craig, thank you for this show and Josh.
卡特和克雷格，谢谢你们观看这个节目，还有乔什。

00:54:31.849 --> 00:54:35.769
Thanks for executing the most imperfect role in the most imperfect way.
感谢你用最不完美的方式演绎了最不完美的角色。

00:54:36.409 --> 00:54:37.124
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

00:54:37.124 --> 00:54:38.672
That's a great compliment.
这是一个很好的赞美。

00:54:38.672 --> 00:54:39.172
Yeah.
是的。

00:54:38.969 --> 00:54:42.520
Ted Mosby is far from perfect, but he's better because he's human.
特德·莫斯比远非完美，但他更好，因为他是人。

00:54:42.520 --> 00:54:44.456
You did a great job portraying that.
你在描绘这一点上做得很好。

00:54:44.456 --> 00:54:46.178
Thank you, thank you, thank you.
谢谢，谢谢，谢谢。

00:54:46.178 --> 00:54:47.361
Wow, that's beautiful.
哇，太漂亮了。

00:54:47.361 --> 00:54:48.329
Thank you, Amanda.
谢谢你，阿曼达。

00:54:48.329 --> 00:54:49.275
Unbelievable.
难以置信。

00:54:49.275 --> 00:54:50.584
Thank you, Amanda.
谢谢你，阿曼达。

00:54:50.584 --> 00:54:52.329
Thank you to all of you.
谢谢大家。

00:54:52.329 --> 00:54:56.652
I just love that the framing of that was like flashback to when I was 19.
我只是喜欢这个框架，就像我 19 岁时的回忆一样。

00:54:56.652 --> 00:54:58.132
By the way, I'm still 19.
顺便说一句，我还19岁。

00:54:58.132 --> 00:55:00.501
I enjoyed the framing of that very much.
我非常喜欢这个框架。

00:55:00.501 --> 00:55:03.876
I remember when I was 19, seven months ago, I'm still 19.
我记得我19岁的时候，七个月前，我还是19岁。

00:55:03.876 --> 00:55:04.376
Okay.
好的。

00:55:04.376 --> 00:55:05.027
I loved it.
我喜欢它。

00:55:05.027 --> 00:55:06.448
Amanda, amazing message.
阿曼达，令人惊奇的消息。

00:55:06.448 --> 00:55:07.573
Thank you for that.
谢谢你。

00:55:07.369 --> 00:55:07.869
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:07.869 --> 00:55:08.369
Fantastic.
极好的。

00:55:08.369 --> 00:55:10.926
Craig, what's it like for you when you hear all this?
克雷格，当你听到这一切时，你有什么感觉？

00:55:12.420 --> 00:55:13.440
It's mind blowing.
真是令人兴奋。

00:55:13.440 --> 00:55:22.619
It's absolutely mind blowing knowing that it helps people get through a hard time And you know, gave them some sort of framing device for their own life in a way.
知道它可以帮助人们度过困难时期，这绝对是令人兴奋的，而且你知道，在某种程度上，它为他们自己的生活提供了某种框架装置。

00:55:22.619 --> 00:55:23.619
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:23.619 --> 00:55:27.619
It's very humbling because we started off here.
这是非常谦卑的，因为我们从这里开始。

00:55:27.619 --> 00:55:29.619
We are at the beginning of talking about this series.
我们正处于谈论这个系列的开始。

00:55:29.619 --> 00:55:31.619
We never could have imagined it with the two messages like that.
我们从来没有想象过会有这样的两条消息。

00:55:31.619 --> 00:55:34.619
It's just deeply humbling and we don't take it lightly.
这真是令人深感谦卑，我们不会掉以轻心。

00:55:34.619 --> 00:55:35.619
Thank you.
谢谢。

00:55:35.619 --> 00:55:44.619
And you know, I think that at your best, at your wildest, at the wildest edges of your imagining of what the show could be, it's that.
你知道，我认为在你最好的、最狂野的、最狂野的边缘，你对这部剧的想象就是这样。

00:55:44.619 --> 00:55:45.619
Right?
正确的？

00:55:45.619 --> 00:55:58.900
No, you make art with the hope, I hope it has it's like a message in a bottle like I hope this reaches someone and I hope the message is not eroded and destroyed by the time it gets there.
不，你带着希望来创作艺术，我希望它就像瓶子里的一条信息一样，我希望这能传达给某人，我希望这条信息在到达那里时不会被侵蚀和破坏。

00:55:59.539 --> 00:56:09.760
There's something so great about you show something and they have the response and beyond even your response, the response of what you would hope.
你展示了一些东西，他们得到了回应，甚至超出了你的回应，这是你所希望的回应。

00:56:09.760 --> 00:56:16.900
I just find it incredibly moving when art is received in such an open-hearted, sincere, beautiful way.
当艺术以如此开放、真诚、美丽的方式被接受时，我感到非常感动。

00:56:16.900 --> 00:56:24.739
It must be really, I mean, we share in it, but you really, you, you and Carter and your team, you know, penned the thing.
我的意思是，这一定是我们共同参与的，但是你真的，你，你和卡特以及你的团队，你知道，写下了这件事。

00:56:24.739 --> 00:56:39.780
So I, I, I just think, um, I hope, I hope other people who are listening to how I met your mother, even, uh, even other people, sorry, who worked on how I met your mother, you know, the props department and the editors and the, you know, I'm sure people who worked on the show are tuning into this.
所以我，我，我只是想，嗯，我希望，我希望其他正在听我如何遇见你母亲的人，甚至，呃，甚至其他人，对不起，那些参与《我如何遇见你母亲》的人，你知道，道具部门和编辑，以及，你知道，我确信参与该剧的人们正在收听这个节目。

00:56:39.780 --> 00:56:46.460
I hope they also feel some sense of, wasn't it incredible to be a part of something this special?
我希望他们也能感受到，成为如此特别的事情的一部分不是很不可思议吗？

00:56:46.460 --> 00:56:51.380
Yeah, everybody put their heart and soul into it and it got a lot of the people who worked on it.
是的，每个人都全身心地投入其中，并且得到了很多人的参与。

00:56:51.380 --> 00:56:55.820
Josh and I included making the show helped us get through some of our hardest times.
乔什和我制作这个节目帮助我们度过了最困难的时期。

00:56:55.820 --> 00:57:00.340
I find it and I find that it just seems like some of that energy made it into the show.
我找到了它，我发现似乎有一些能量融入到了这部剧中。

00:57:00.340 --> 00:57:20.982
The show was that to us and creating it in real time and now people years and years later and people who are 19 years old and going through their own hard time are are feeling that in the show and it just makes me feel like we baked we baked something in there that's lasting.
这个节目对我们来说就是这样，而且是实时创作的，现在人们在很多年以后，那些19岁的人正在经历自己的艰难时期，他们在节目中感受到了这一点，这让我觉得我们在里面烘焙了一些持久的东西。

00:57:20.982 --> 00:57:36.539
Yeah and also this notion of watching characters go through hard times with this sense of chosen family and community and that they landed on their feet and they were able to laugh in the midst of hard times.
是的，还有这种观看角色经历艰难时期的观念，带着这种选择家庭和社区的感觉，他们站起来，能够在艰难时期中欢笑。

00:57:36.539 --> 00:57:37.039
Yeah.
是的。

00:57:37.039 --> 00:57:52.746
Like how am I my mother was still it was brightly lit it was trot on a soundstage there's laughter piped in it was it was a fantasy but it also was attempting to gesture at something very true about Dave Alive.
就像我怎么了，我的母亲仍然一样，它灯火通明，在摄影棚里小跑，里面传出笑声，这是一个幻想，但它也试图表现出关于戴夫·艾利夫的一些非常真实的东西。

